  "hints": [
    "A palindrome ending at a position can extend an optimal partition of the prefix before it.",
    "Maintain minimum cuts for prefixes and discover palindromes by expanding odd and even centers.",
    "Initialize cuts[i]=i-1. For each palindrome s[left:right+1], minimize cuts[right+1] with cuts[left]+1.",
    "The empty prefix has -1 cuts so a palindrome starting at index zero gives zero, not one."
  ],
  "editorial": "Expand both possible center types and update prefix-cut minima for each discovered palindrome. Processing centers left-to-right ensures the prefix ending before a candidate palindrome has already received all relevant updates: its palindromes have earlier centers. The special empty-prefix cost -1 accounts for the fact that the first piece requires no preceding cut. The method uses O(n) storage and O(n²) comparisons in the worst case. The independent oracle explicitly enumerates all cut masks and checks every resulting piece on small inputs.",
